{
  "id": "u12-l02",
  "unit": "u12-have-to",
  "title": "I have to",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**'Have to' = -তে form + হবে.** The person who has to do it goes in the **-কে** form, not আমি:\n\n- **আমাকে যেতে হবে।** 'I have to go.'\n- **তোমাকে, আপনাকে, তাকে, ওকে, ওনাকে** + -তে + **হবে**\n\nFor আমরা use **আমাদের**: **আমাদের এখন ঘুমাতে হবে** 'We have to sleep now'.\n\n**হবে never changes**, whoever has to do it: **আপনাকে আসতে হবে**.\n\n*আমি যেতে হবে* is the most common learner mistake. Think of it as 'to me, going will be (needed)'.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "hobe-must",
      "bn": "হবে",
      "tr": "hobe",
      "en": "have to (after a -তে verb)",
      "notes": "X-কে + infinitive + হবে: আমাকে যেতে হবে \"I have to go\". Same word as হবে \"will be\"; the verb never changes for the person."
    },
    {
      "id": "uthte",
      "bn": "উঠতে",
      "tr": "uthte",
      "en": "to get up",
      "notes": "Infinitive of ওঠা; the stem is উঠ- as in উঠি."
    },
    {
      "id": "ghumate",
      "bn": "ঘুমাতে",
      "tr": "ghumate",
      "en": "to sleep",
      "notes": "Infinitive of ঘুমানো: ঘুমাই → ঘুমাতে. Kolkata ঘুমোতে."
    },
    {
      "id": "taratari",
      "bn": "তাড়াতাড়ি",
      "tr": "taratari",
      "en": "early",
      "notes": "তাড়াতাড়ি উঠতে হবে \"have to get up early\"; তাড়াতাড়ি আসো \"come quickly\"."
    },
    {
      "id": "oke",
      "bn": "ওকে",
      "tr": "oke",
      "en": "him/her (spoken)",
      "notes": "Object form of ও: ওকে যেতে হবে \"he/she has to go\"."
    },
    {
      "id": "onake",
      "bn": "ওনাকে",
      "tr": "onake",
      "en": "him/her (polite)",
      "notes": "Object form of উনি: ওনাকে আসতে হবে."
    }
  ],
